+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository layer
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents, createdAt)` that updates the order's `discount_cents`/`final_amount_cents`/`coupon_code` and, in the same `BEGIN`/`COMMIT` transaction, inserts the `coupon_redemptions` row and increments `coupons.used_count`; verify with a repository-level check that all three writes land or none do (`npm test`).
+- [x] 1.2 Add a `CouponRepository.findByCode` based eligibility read path needs no new SQL; confirm the existing `findByCode` returns every field the service needs (`usedCount`, `usageLimit`, `validFrom`, `validUntil`, `minAmountCents`, `maxDiscountCents`).
+
+## 2. Service logic
+
+- [x] 2.1 Inject `CouponRepository` into `OrderService` and wire it in `src/app.ts`; verify `npm run build` type-checks.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` with the fixed validation order from design.md (couponCode shape → order exists → `PENDING` → no coupon → coupon exists → `ACTIVE` → validity window vs `clock()` → `minAmountCents` → `usageLimit`); verify each rejection returns its documented code in the new tests.
+- [x] 2.3 Implement discount math (FIXED = value, PERCENT = `Math.floor(amount * value / 100)`, then `maxDiscountCents` cap, then clamp to `amountCents`) and return the updated order; verify FIXED, PERCENT, capped, and over-amount cases match the spec scenarios.
+
+## 3. HTTP layer and tests
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` returning 200 with the updated order; verify a request through `createApp().request(...)` returns the discounted order.
+- [x] 3.2 Add tests covering the happy path for FIXED and PERCENT, the `maxDiscountCents` cap, over-amount clamping, `usedCount` increment, and the redemption row; verify `npm test` passes.
+- [x] 3.3 Add tests covering each rejection: `INVALID_REQUEST`, `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`, `ORDER_ALREADY_HAS_COUPON`, `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`, `COUPON_DISABLED`, `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID`, `COUPON_EXPIRED`, `COUPON_MIN_AMOUNT_NOT_MET`, `COUPON_USAGE_LIMIT_REACHED`, plus the no-side-effects-on-failure guarantee; verify `npm test` passes and `npm run build` succeeds.
+
+## 4. Integration check
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run the full suite (`npm run build && npm test`) and confirm the pre-existing `tests/orders.test.ts` behavior is unchanged and the new endpoint works end to end.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after review, and verify the archived spec lands under `openspec/specs/order-coupons/`.
